"Three elections, three majorities, and not a single speechwriter in Canberra left doubting the formula. The boy from the Camperdown council flats who built a career out of never getting ahead of the room has now joined Bob Hawke as a Labor leader with three straight wins—not with sweeping ideological crusades, but by making himself harder to dislodge than the furniture. In the party room tonight, the talk is no longer about who succeeds him, but how long he intends to stay.",
"Three terms, and each one bigger than the last. Anthony Albanese becomes one of the rare prime ministers to grow his majority at two elections in a row, turning an electorate braced for volatility into a Labor fortress.",
