"Hanson's {on} seats are not enough to unseat the Coalition as Opposition or hold the government to ransom, but across regional Queensland and the outer suburbs One Nation has redrawn the political map.",
"With {on} seats in the House—up from {before}—Pauline Hanson finishes third behind a {government} majority, commanding a sizable regional party room even without balance-of-power leverage.",
"A {government} majority denies Pauline Hanson the kingmaker role she campaigned for, yet her {on} lower-house MPs give One Nation its strongest parliamentary foothold since the party was founded."
